---
// The terms of using Kemable. The licenses themselves are LICENSE and LICENSING.md in the repository
// (docs/decisions/0023-licensing.md); this page points to them and never restates them.
import DraftNotice from "../components/DraftNotice.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT, REPOSITORY } from "../links";
---

<Base title="Terms of Service · Kemable" description="The terms of using Kemable, and the licenses it is offered under.">
  <article class="prose-page">
    <DraftNotice />
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p>Last updated 15 November 2026.</p>

    <p>
      Kemable is a database client for Windows, made by Huỳnh Trung Đức as a SoleBuilt project. These terms cover the app and this website. By
      installing or using Kemable you accept them.
    </p>

    <h2>The license</h2>
    <p>
      Kemable is open source under the <a href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only</a> (AGPL-3.0).
      You may use, study, change and share it under that license. If you share it, changed or not, or let others use a changed version over a
      network, you must offer them its source under the same license.
    </p>
    <p>
      Kemable is also offered under a commercial license, for anyone who wants to use it without the AGPL's conditions, for example inside a product
      whose source stays closed. Its terms are not published yet. <a href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/LICENSING.md`}>LICENSING.md</a> says which
      license covers what, and how to ask about the commercial one.
    </p>
    <p>
      The libraries and fonts inside the app keep their own licenses. Their notices are installed beside the app, and Settings › About opens them.
    </p>

    <h2>The name and the logo</h2>
    <p>
      The names Kemable and SoleBuilt and the Kemable icon and logo are not covered by the licenses above. <a
        href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/TRADEMARKS.md`}>TRADEMARKS.md</a
      > says how you may use them.
    </p>

    <h2>Your data and your servers</h2>
    <p>
      Kemable connects only to the servers you point it at, with the credentials you give it, and runs the statements you run. You are responsible
      for having the right to reach those servers and for what you change on them. Kemable shows the statements an edit, an import or a drop will
      run before it runs them; read them before you confirm. Keep backups of data that matters.
    </p>
    <p>What the app sends and keeps is in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>
      At launch Kemable checks GitHub for a newer version and asks you before installing it. Updates are signed; the app installs only an installer
      whose signature matches. You can turn the check off in Settings › Updates.
    </p>

    <h2>Preview software</h2>
    <p>
      Kemable is in preview. Features may change or be removed between versions, and some engines are marked as previews in the app. Report a
      problem on <a href={`${REPOSITORY}/issues`}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      Kemable is provided as is, without any warranty, to the extent the law allows, as section 15 of the AGPL-3.0 says. To the extent the law allows,
      the author is not liable for any loss or damage from using it, including lost or corrupted data, as section 16 of the AGPL-3.0 says. A
      commercial license may give other terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change with a new version of the app. The date above says when they last did, and the history of this page is public in <a
        href={REPOSITORY}>Kemable's repository</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
